{"id":"vol8-03","section":4,"path":"bank/listening/vol8-03/audio-4.m4a","model":"small","duration":297.1,"segments":[{"start":0.0,"end":2.98,"text":"Now turn to section 4 on page 7.","words":[["Now",0.0,0.24],["turn",0.24,0.58],["to",0.58,0.76],["section",0.76,1.02],["4",1.02,1.58],["on",1.58,2.18],["page",2.18,2.48],["7.",2.48,2.98]]},{"start":5.6,"end":6.48,"text":"Section 4.","words":[["Section",5.6,5.9],["4.",5.9,6.48]]},{"start":7.64,"end":13.48,"text":"You will hear part of a presentation given by a business student on an assignment about","words":[["You",7.64,7.72],["will",7.72,7.9],["hear",7.9,8.16],["part",8.16,8.54],["of",8.54,8.7],["a",8.7,8.8],["presentation",8.8,9.34],["given",9.34,10.04],["by",10.04,10.42],["a",10.42,10.62],["business",10.62,10.82],["student",10.82,11.54],["on",11.54,12.34],["an",12.34,12.46],["assignment",12.46,12.98],["about",12.98,13.48]]},{"start":13.48,"end":15.34,"text":"absence from work.","words":[["absence",13.48,14.36],["from",14.36,14.84],["work.",14.84,15.34]]},{"start":16.18,"end":22.04,"text":"First, you have some time to look at questions 31 to 40 on page 7.","words":[["First,",16.18,16.62],["you",17.08,17.24],["have",17.24,17.42],["some",17.42,17.62],["time",17.62,18.0],["to",18.0,18.18],["look",18.18,18.3],["at",18.3,18.46],["questions",18.46,18.8],["31",18.8,19.72],["to",19.72,20.02],["40",20.02,20.48],["on",20.48,21.22],["page",21.22,21.54],["7.",21.54,22.04]]},{"start":72.35,"end":76.37,"text":"Now listen carefully and answer questions 31 to 40.","words":[["Now",72.35,72.61],["listen",72.61,72.91],["carefully",72.91,73.31],["and",73.31,74.03],["answer",74.03,74.39],["questions",74.39,74.79],["31",74.79,75.73],["to",75.73,75.99],["40.",75.99,76.37]]},{"start":76.37,"end":84.55,"text":"Hello, everyone. For my assignment, I did a review of the literature concerning absence","words":[["Hello,",76.37,77.47],["everyone.",80.25,80.43],["For",81.19,81.39],["my",81.39,81.59],["assignment,",81.59,82.05],["I",82.27,82.31],["did",82.31,82.43],["a",82.43,82.55],["review",82.55,82.83],["of",82.83,83.07],["the",83.07,83.17],["literature",83.17,83.55],["concerning",83.55,84.09],["absence",84.09,84.55]]},{"start":84.55,"end":89.97,"text":"in the workplace, and I'm going to present a summary of what I found. I looked at some","words":[["in",84.55,84.85],["the",84.85,84.95],["workplace,",84.95,85.17],["and",85.67,86.23],["I'm",86.23,86.45],["going",86.45,86.59],["to",86.59,86.73],["present",86.73,86.95],["a",86.95,87.13],["summary",87.13,87.45],["of",87.45,87.59],["what",87.59,87.67],["I",87.67,87.79],["found.",87.79,88.09],["I",89.21,89.49],["looked",89.49,89.65],["at",89.65,89.81],["some",89.81,89.97]]},{"start":89.97,"end":95.41,"text":"research on absence from work, that is, the number of days work people miss for various","words":[["research",89.97,90.39],["on",90.39,90.67],["absence",90.67,91.03],["from",91.03,91.31],["work,",91.31,91.57],["that",92.07,92.29],["is,",92.29,92.53],["the",92.89,92.99],["number",92.99,93.23],["of",93.23,93.39],["days",93.39,93.65],["work",93.65,94.03],["people",94.03,94.41],["miss",94.41,94.85],["for",94.85,95.13],["various",95.13,95.41]]},{"start":95.41,"end":101.81,"text":"reasons. Researchers refer to two types of absence, frequent absence, which is obviously","words":[["reasons.",95.41,95.85],["Researchers",96.65,97.07],["refer",97.07,97.43],["to",97.43,97.71],["two",97.71,97.93],["types",97.93,98.31],["of",98.31,98.57],["absence,",98.57,98.93],["frequent",99.63,100.05],["absence,",100.05,100.43],["which",100.93,101.15],["is",101.15,101.39],["obviously",101.39,101.81]]},{"start":101.81,"end":107.95,"text":"a more serious problem, and occasional absence. A lot of studies look at the factors involved","words":[["a",101.81,101.99],["more",101.99,102.07],["serious",102.07,102.39],["problem,",102.39,102.91],["and",103.39,103.69],["occasional",103.69,104.13],["absence.",104.13,104.63],["A",105.63,105.97],["lot",105.97,106.11],["of",106.11,106.25],["studies",106.25,106.47],["look",106.47,106.79],["at",106.79,106.97],["the",106.97,107.07],["factors",107.07,107.39],["involved",107.39,107.95]]},{"start":107.95,"end":110.95,"text":"involved in absence from work, and several have been identified.","words":[["involved",107.95,108.07],["in",108.07,108.19],["absence",108.19,108.51],["from",108.51,108.81],["work,",108.81,109.09],["and",109.49,109.77],["several",109.77,110.13],["have",110.13,110.39],["been",110.39,110.53],["identified.",110.53,110.95]]},{"start":111.87,"end":117.37,"text":"Firstly, the gender of the employee may influence his or her ability to attend work.","words":[["Firstly,",111.87,112.21],["the",112.87,113.01],["gender",113.01,113.37],["of",113.37,113.61],["the",113.61,113.73],["employee",113.73,114.19],["may",114.19,114.81],["influence",114.81,115.25],["his",115.25,115.53],["or",115.53,115.81],["her",115.81,116.05],["ability",116.05,116.51],["to",116.51,116.73],["attend",116.73,117.03],["work.",117.03,117.37]]},{"start":118.01,"end":122.35,"text":"For example, a female is more likely to have childcare responsibility,","words":[["For",118.01,118.17],["example,",118.17,118.53],["a",119.09,119.19],["female",119.19,119.49],["is",119.49,120.25],["more",120.25,120.45],["likely",120.45,120.79],["to",120.79,120.93],["have",120.93,121.11],["childcare",121.11,121.59],["responsibility,",121.59,122.35]]},{"start":123.07,"end":125.37,"text":"and so could be absent as a result of that.","words":[["and",123.07,123.45],["so",123.45,123.67],["could",123.67,123.93],["be",123.93,124.13],["absent",124.13,124.43],["as",124.43,124.71],["a",124.71,124.79],["result",124.79,125.01],["of",125.01,125.19],["that.",125.19,125.37]]},{"start":126.01,"end":131.35,"text":"The next factor that has been identified is the attitude of employees toward their work.","words":[["The",126.01,126.39],["next",126.39,126.55],["factor",126.55,126.95],["that",126.95,127.37],["has",127.37,127.53],["been",127.53,127.71],["identified",127.71,128.25],["is",128.25,129.03],["the",129.03,129.17],["attitude",129.17,129.59],["of",129.59,129.81],["employees",129.81,130.31],["toward",130.31,130.79],["their",130.79,131.01],["work.",131.01,131.35]]},{"start":131.35,"end":137.21,"text":"But there has been a lot of debate about the extent to which this actually does influence","words":[["But",131.35,132.33],["there",132.33,132.53],["has",132.53,132.69],["been",132.69,132.87],["a",132.87,132.97],["lot",132.97,133.13],["of",133.13,133.27],["debate",133.27,133.61],["about",133.61,134.47],["the",134.47,134.67],["extent",134.67,135.03],["to",135.03,135.27],["which",135.27,135.47],["this",135.47,135.97],["actually",135.97,136.47],["does",136.47,136.69],["influence",136.69,137.21]]},{"start":137.21,"end":141.55,"text":"absence, and some people argue that the research hasn't been conclusive.","words":[["absence,",137.21,137.69],["and",138.05,138.61],["some",138.61,138.85],["people",138.85,139.09],["argue",139.09,139.45],["that",139.45,140.09],["the",140.09,140.21],["research",140.21,140.55],["hasn't",140.55,140.93],["been",140.93,141.05],["conclusive.",141.05,141.55]]},{"start":142.79,"end":148.05,"text":"Some researchers have suggested that another reason for high levels of absence is that","words":[["Some",142.79,143.13],["researchers",143.13,143.67],["have",143.67,143.95],["suggested",143.95,144.49],["that",144.49,145.17],["another",145.17,145.39],["reason",145.39,145.81],["for",145.81,145.97],["high",145.97,146.27],["levels",146.27,146.61],["of",146.61,146.81],["absence",146.81,147.19],["is",147.19,147.89],["that",147.89,148.05]]},{"start":148.05,"end":153.53,"text":"some organizations have a culture in which absence is accepted, that others have criticized","words":[["some",148.05,148.31],["organizations",148.31,148.83],["have",148.83,149.41],["a",149.41,149.51],["culture",149.51,149.87],["in",149.87,150.53],["which",150.53,150.67],["absence",150.67,151.09],["is",151.09,151.35],["accepted,",151.35,151.79],["that",152.57,152.71],["others",152.71,152.91],["have",152.91,153.15],["criticized",153.15,153.53]]},{"start":153.53,"end":157.13,"text":"this model, arguing that it's too much of a generalization.","words":[["this",153.53,153.97],["model,",153.97,154.31],["arguing",154.89,155.17],["that",155.17,155.77],["it's",155.77,155.89],["too",155.89,156.03],["much",156.03,156.31],["of",156.31,156.43],["a",156.43,156.51],["generalization.",156.51,157.13]]},{"start":157.91,"end":162.13,"text":"And then, there are factors related to the type of work the employee does.","words":[["And",157.91,158.51],["then,",158.51,158.79],["there",159.05,159.31],["are",159.31,159.43],["factors",159.43,159.73],["related",159.73,160.13],["to",160.13,160.39],["the",160.39,160.51],["type",160.51,160.81],["of",160.81,161.03],["work",161.03,161.23],["the",161.23,161.43],["employee",161.43,161.79],["does.",161.79,162.13]]},{"start":163.11,"end":167.81,"text":"It's been claimed that workers in industry are more likely to have high absence rates","words":[["It's",163.11,163.39],["been",163.39,163.53],["claimed",163.53,163.87],["that",163.87,164.09],["workers",164.09,164.39],["in",164.39,164.63],["industry",164.63,165.11],["are",165.11,165.83],["more",165.83,166.01],["likely",166.01,166.31],["to",166.31,166.43],["have",166.43,166.71],["high",166.71,167.01],["absence",167.01,167.35],["rates",167.35,167.81]]},{"start":168.15,"end":169.65,"text":"than people who work in offices.","words":[["than",168.15,168.45],["people",168.45,168.71],["who",168.71,168.91],["work",168.91,169.15],["in",169.15,169.31],["offices.",169.31,169.65]]},{"start":170.77,"end":175.85,"text":"It's also important to recognize that groups within a single organization might behave","words":[["It's",170.77,171.07],["also",171.07,171.27],["important",171.27,171.79],["to",171.79,171.99],["recognize",171.99,172.45],["that",172.45,173.15],["groups",173.15,173.35],["within",173.35,173.67],["a",173.67,173.83],["single",173.83,174.11],["organization",174.11,174.85],["might",174.85,175.47],["behave",175.47,175.85]]},{"start":175.85,"end":176.17,"text":"differently.","words":[["differently.",175.85,176.17]]},{"start":176.95,"end":181.75,"text":"For example, one of the other underlying themes in the literature is that there is","words":[["For",176.95,177.13],["example,",177.13,177.51],["one",178.15,178.43],["of",178.43,178.53],["the",178.53,178.63],["other",178.63,178.77],["underlying",178.77,179.29],["themes",179.29,179.79],["in",179.79,180.11],["the",180.11,180.21],["literature",180.21,180.59],["is",180.59,181.31],["that",181.31,181.43],["there",181.43,181.61],["is",181.61,181.75]]},{"start":181.75,"end":187.15,"text":"a connection between how often an employee is absent and what size of workgroup he or","words":[["a",181.75,181.87],["connection",181.87,182.19],["between",182.19,182.61],["how",182.61,182.95],["often",182.95,183.29],["an",183.29,183.41],["employee",183.41,183.79],["is",183.79,184.03],["absent",184.03,184.39],["and",184.39,185.21],["what",185.21,185.39],["size",185.39,185.81],["of",185.81,186.11],["workgroup",186.11,186.65],["he",186.65,186.97],["or",186.97,187.15]]},{"start":187.15,"end":192.95,"text":"she belongs to. Specifically, it's been found that the bigger the group, the higher the","words":[["she",187.15,187.39],["belongs",187.39,187.77],["to.",187.77,188.03],["Specifically,",188.75,189.23],["it's",189.93,190.17],["been",190.17,190.29],["found",190.29,190.63],["that",190.63,190.85],["the",190.85,190.97],["bigger",190.97,191.21],["the",191.21,191.35],["group,",191.35,191.69],["the",192.17,192.39],["higher",192.39,192.73],["the",192.73,192.95]]},{"start":192.95,"end":203.16,"text":"levels of absence. On a related theme, some writers have focused on a comparison between","words":[["levels",192.95,193.25],["of",193.25,193.41],["absence.",193.41,193.75],["On",199.0,199.3],["a",199.3,199.4],["related",199.4,199.68],["theme,",199.68,200.1],["some",200.6,200.78],["writers",200.78,201.1],["have",201.1,201.34],["focused",201.34,201.7],["on",201.7,202.12],["a",202.12,202.2],["comparison",202.2,202.8],["between",202.8,203.16]]},{"start":203.16,"end":208.78,"text":"public sector organizations and private sector ones. There is some evidence that absence","words":[["public",203.16,203.56],["sector",203.56,203.92],["organizations",203.92,204.36],["and",204.36,205.3],["private",205.3,205.7],["sector",205.7,206.06],["ones.",206.06,206.36],["There",207.0,207.3],["is",207.3,207.46],["some",207.46,207.68],["evidence",207.68,208.04],["that",208.04,208.42],["absence",208.42,208.78]]},{"start":208.78,"end":213.96,"text":"levels are higher in the public sector. It's not exactly clear why this should","words":[["levels",208.78,209.24],["are",209.24,209.88],["higher",209.88,210.22],["in",210.22,210.56],["the",210.56,210.64],["public",210.64,210.86],["sector.",210.86,211.22],["It's",211.86,212.3],["not",212.3,212.44],["exactly",212.44,212.86],["clear",212.86,213.22],["why",213.22,213.56],["this",213.56,213.8],["should",213.8,213.96]]},{"start":213.96,"end":220.54,"text":"be the case. But one explanation that has been often put forward is that in some cases, public","words":[["be",213.96,214.08],["the",214.08,214.22],["case.",214.22,214.56],["But",215.22,215.44],["one",215.44,215.68],["explanation",215.68,216.28],["that",216.28,216.68],["has",216.68,216.86],["been",216.86,217.0],["often",217.0,217.36],["put",217.36,217.62],["forward",217.62,218.02],["is",218.02,218.84],["that",218.84,219.04],["in",219.04,219.14],["some",219.14,219.38],["cases,",219.38,219.9],["public",220.26,220.54]]},{"start":220.54,"end":226.54,"text":"sector organizations may not be as efficient. This might be because their systems are more","words":[["sector",220.54,220.9],["organizations",220.9,221.42],["may",221.42,222.34],["not",222.34,222.54],["be",222.54,222.74],["as",222.74,222.86],["efficient.",222.86,223.2],["This",223.94,224.38],["might",224.38,224.58],["be",224.58,224.8],["because",224.8,225.18],["their",225.18,225.44],["systems",225.44,225.96],["are",225.96,226.34],["more",226.34,226.54]]},{"start":226.54,"end":232.8,"text":"bureaucratic due to factors which are external rather than internal, like the degree of control","words":[["bureaucratic",226.54,227.2],["due",227.2,228.0],["to",228.0,228.14],["factors",228.14,228.5],["which",228.5,228.82],["are",228.82,229.04],["external",229.04,229.66],["rather",229.66,230.3],["than",230.3,230.52],["internal,",230.52,231.08],["like",231.62,231.88],["the",231.88,232.0],["degree",232.0,232.24],["of",232.24,232.38],["control",232.38,232.8]]},{"start":232.8,"end":237.9,"text":"the government imposes on the public sector. However, most recent literature suggests","words":[["the",232.8,232.98],["government",232.98,233.2],["imposes",233.2,233.7],["on",233.7,234.14],["the",234.14,234.28],["public",234.28,234.5],["sector.",234.5,234.9],["However,",235.64,236.02],["most",236.22,236.68],["recent",236.68,237.02],["literature",237.02,237.34],["suggests",237.34,237.9]]},{"start":237.9,"end":239.58,"text":"a number of other explanations.","words":[["a",237.9,238.36],["number",238.36,238.64],["of",238.64,238.78],["other",238.78,239.0],["explanations.",239.0,239.58]]},{"start":240.28,"end":242.86,"text":"Firstly, a public sector organization","words":[["Firstly,",240.28,240.66],["a",241.4,241.52],["public",241.52,241.8],["sector",241.8,242.14],["organization",242.14,242.86]]},{"start":242.86,"end":245.46,"text":"tends to have a workforce which is larger.","words":[["tends",242.86,243.64],["to",243.64,243.86],["have",243.86,244.12],["a",244.12,244.28],["workforce",244.28,244.6],["which",244.6,244.98],["is",244.98,245.12],["larger.",245.12,245.46]]},{"start":246.2,"end":250.54,"text":"Also, it tends to employ a higher number of female and older employees,","words":[["Also,",246.2,246.56],["it",247.12,247.24],["tends",247.24,247.46],["to",247.46,247.64],["employ",247.64,248.0],["a",248.0,248.2],["higher",248.2,248.48],["number",248.48,248.78],["of",248.78,248.94],["female",248.94,249.24],["and",249.24,249.56],["older",249.56,249.9],["employees,",249.9,250.54]]},{"start":251.0,"end":254.6,"text":"both of which groups are likely to record higher absence rates.","words":[["both",251.0,251.24],["of",251.24,251.42],["which",251.42,251.6],["groups",251.6,251.96],["are",251.96,252.48],["likely",252.48,252.8],["to",252.8,252.96],["record",252.96,253.34],["higher",253.34,253.72],["absence",253.72,254.16],["rates.",254.16,254.6]]},{"start":255.58,"end":258.6,"text":"It is also suggested that public sector organizations","words":[["It",255.58,255.96],["is",255.96,256.06],["also",256.06,256.3],["suggested",256.3,256.84],["that",256.84,257.38],["public",257.38,257.7],["sector",257.7,258.06],["organizations",258.06,258.6]]},{"start":258.6,"end":263.14,"text":"are more likely to give their absent employees benefits for a longer period","words":[["are",258.6,259.26],["more",259.26,259.44],["likely",259.44,259.78],["to",259.78,259.94],["give",259.94,260.14],["their",260.14,260.34],["absent",260.34,260.68],["employees",260.68,261.26],["benefits",261.26,261.84],["for",261.84,262.4],["a",262.4,262.52],["longer",262.52,262.7],["period",262.7,263.14]]},{"start":263.14,"end":266.6,"text":"and are less likely to place restrictions on these.","words":[["and",263.14,264.02],["are",264.02,264.14],["less",264.14,264.34],["likely",264.34,264.74],["to",264.74,265.3],["place",265.3,265.5],["restrictions",265.5,266.02],["on",266.02,266.34],["these.",266.34,266.6]]},{"start":266.6,"end":274.16,"text":"In addition, it's been found that public sector employers have less of a tendency to dismiss employees for being absent.","words":[["In",266.6,267.56],["addition,",267.56,267.9],["it's",268.6,268.7],["been",268.7,268.82],["found",268.82,269.14],["that",269.14,269.32],["public",269.32,269.58],["sector",269.58,269.94],["employers",269.94,270.42],["have",270.42,271.26],["less",271.26,271.54],["of",271.54,271.78],["a",271.78,271.9],["tendency",271.9,272.14],["to",272.14,272.42],["dismiss",272.42,272.7],["employees",272.7,273.28],["for",273.28,273.54],["being",273.54,273.76],["absent.",273.76,274.16]]},{"start":275.04,"end":280.86,"text":"And all of these could be additional or alternative reasons for higher absence rates in the public sector.","words":[["And",275.04,275.28],["all",275.28,275.44],["of",275.44,275.56],["these",275.56,275.74],["could",275.74,275.98],["be",275.98,276.12],["additional",276.12,276.64],["or",276.64,276.98],["alternative",276.98,277.46],["reasons",277.46,278.02],["for",278.02,278.56],["higher",278.56,278.84],["absence",278.84,279.24],["rates",279.24,279.76],["in",279.76,280.22],["the",280.22,280.3],["public",280.3,280.5],["sector.",280.5,280.86]]},{"start":281.88,"end":284.74,"text":"Now, I'd like to talk about the management of absences.","words":[["Now,",281.88,282.12],["I'd",282.52,282.74],["like",282.74,282.84],["to",282.84,282.96],["talk",282.96,283.16],["about",283.16,283.46],["the",283.46,283.64],["management",283.64,284.04],["of",284.04,284.3],["absences.",284.3,284.74]]},{"start":288.1,"end":293.06,"text":"That is the end of section 4. You now have half a minute to check your answers.","words":[["That",288.1,288.52],["is",288.52,288.68],["the",288.68,288.82],["end",288.82,289.04],["of",289.04,289.16],["section",289.16,289.42],["4.",289.42,289.96],["You",290.78,290.96],["now",290.96,291.18],["have",291.18,291.42],["half",291.42,291.7],["a",291.7,291.84],["minute",291.84,291.98],["to",291.98,292.18],["check",292.18,292.44],["your",292.44,292.68],["answers.",292.68,293.06]]}]}